---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

// Canonical copy of the terms of service — the web app's /terms-of-service
// route redirects here. Intentionally English-only: a single authoritative
// document, linked from the Chrome Web Store listing and the Google OAuth
// consent screen.
---

<Base
  title='Terms of Service — Flicktionary'
  description='The terms that govern your use of Flicktionary.'
>
  <main class='mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 px-6 py-12 text-gray-800'>
    <header class='space-y-2'>
      <h1 class='text-3xl font-bold'>Flicktionary Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class='text-sm text-gray-500'>Last updated: June 3, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>1. Agreement to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        Flicktionary (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) is a language-learning service consisting of the web app at
        flicktionary.app and a companion browser extension (together, the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;). By creating an account
        or using the Service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>2. Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You must provide accurate information when creating an account and keep your sign-in credentials secure. You are
        responsible for all activity that occurs under your account. You must be at least 13 years old (or the minimum
        age required to consent to data processing in your country) to use the Service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>3. Subscriptions and payment</h2>
      <ul class='list-disc space-y-2 pl-6'>
        <li>
          Some features of the Service require a paid subscription. Payment is processed by Stripe; prices and billing
          periods are shown at the time of purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          Subscriptions renew automatically at the end of each billing period unless you cancel beforehand. You can
          cancel at any time from your account settings; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing
          period, and you keep access to paid features until then.
        </li>
        <li>
          We may change subscription prices. Price changes apply from your next billing period, and we will notify you
          in advance so you can cancel if you do not accept the new price.
        </li>
        <li>Except where required by law, payments are non-refundable.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>4. Your content</h2>
      <p>
        The Service lets you save words and phrases, make notes and highlights, and import or paste text (for example
        subtitles of a video you watch or an article you import). You retain ownership of the content you submit. You
        grant us the limited license needed to operate the Service: to store your content, process it (including with AI
        language-model providers such as Anthropic) to generate the definitions, explanations, and study material you
        request, and display it back to you. We do not use your content to train AI models, and we do not share it with
        other users.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the content you submit. Only import or save material you are legally permitted to use
        for your personal study.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>5. AI-generated content</h2>
      <p>
        Definitions, explanations, translations, and study material are generated by AI language models. They are
        provided as a learning aid and may occasionally be inaccurate or incomplete. Do not rely on them where accuracy
        is critical, and use your own judgment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>6. Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul class='list-disc space-y-2 pl-6'>
        <li>Do not use the Service for anything unlawful or to infringe the rights of others.</li>
        <li>
          Do not attempt to disrupt or gain unauthorized access to the Service, probe or circumvent its security, or
          interfere with other users&rsquo; use of it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not scrape the Service, access it through automated means other than the official apps, or resell it
          without our written permission.
        </li>
        <li>Do not abuse the AI features, including attempting to extract the underlying models or prompts.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms.</p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>7. Third-party content and services</h2>
      <p>
        The browser extension works alongside third-party websites and streaming services. We are not affiliated with
        those services, and these terms do not modify your agreements with them. You are responsible for complying with
        the terms of the websites you use the extension on.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Service, including its software, design, and branding, is owned by us or our licensors and is protected by
        intellectual-property laws. These terms do not grant you any rights to it other than the right to use the
        Service as intended.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>9. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can stop using the Service and delete your account at any time from your profile settings, which permanently
        and irreversibly removes your account information and learning data. We may suspend or terminate your access if
        you violate these terms or if we discontinue the Service; if we discontinue a paid service, we will refund the
        unused portion of your subscription.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>10. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo;, without warranties of any kind,
        whether express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not guarantee
        that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that the learning material it produces is accurate.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or
        consequential damages arising from your use of the Service, and our total liability for any claim is limited to
        the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim arose. Nothing in these terms excludes liability
        that cannot be excluded under applicable law, including your statutory rights as a consumer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. We will post any changes on this page and update the &ldquo;Last
        updated&rdquo; date above; for material changes we will notify you through the Service or by email. Continuing
        to use the Service after changes take effect means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class='space-y-3'>
      <h2 class='text-xl font-semibold'>13. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email us at{' '}
        <a class='text-blue-600 underline' href='mailto:support@flicktionary.app'>support@flicktionary.app</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
